		(uuid "23fa7b93-d8b8-49ee-b71d-b7c4a8f96721")
	)
	(text "NOTES\n1. U301 at a board edge, as on ST's reference PCB (DS14096 fig. 6): copper-free notch past the antenna end.\n2. C301-C303 at the VDD pads; C304 at NRST.\n3. PB0/PB1/PB2 left unconnected (ST: RF-sensitive pins). NTC_EN = PA8, EN_5V1 = PA11, EN_5V2 = PA12.\n4. R303 0R joins ANT_IN/ANT_OUT for the internal antenna (ST fig. 2).\n5. Pin map checked against DS13258 table 15: NTC ADC1_IN6/8/9/10, IRQs on WKUP1/WKUP4, I2C1, USART1.\n   PB4 = 3V3_SLEEP: PB4 resets as NJTRST with pull-up, so the 3V3 rail boots in normal mode;\n   firmware makes PB4 a GPIO output before using sleep mode. PB5 = LED, PA6 = GAUGE_BTP.\n6. R307 removes the LED for sleep-current measurements.\n7. Diamonds are PWR_FLAGs (ERC only, no part): each sits where its rail is sourced through a passive part.\n8. SW301 resets the MCU. TP306 is BOOT0: hold it at 3V3 while releasing reset for the UART bootloader.\n9. R313 (DNP) holds 3V3_SLEEP high (normal mode) while the MCU is off. TP307 probes it.\n10. R312 feeds the SMBus pull-ups: remove it and supply TP308 for EV2400 work while 3V3 is down.\n11. R316-R319: J303 can override NTC_EN/EN_5V1/EN_5V2/CHG_INH without shorting the MCU outputs.\n12. PB8 = CHG_INH: drive high to stop both chargers (gauge silent, implausible or wrongly configured; FET stuck on)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 287.02 213.36 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
